cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "QSVT: A First-Principles C++ Framework for Quantum Singular Value Transformation"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch C++ implementation of Quantum Singular Value Transformation
  that compiles a matrix function f(A) into a runnable quantum circuit. It
  includes an embeddable, dependency-free QSP phase-angle solver — the
  symmetric-QSP Newton method plus an inverse nonlinear Fourier transform, with
  the crossover between them measured rather than assumed — a QSP target
  compiler that returns validated angles or an actionable reason none exist,
  LCU block encoding with native-gate synthesis, and OpenQASM export. The core
  is stdlib-only C++17, verified in CI by compiling it with no include paths at
  all and linking it from pure C.
type: software
